{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app","sessionId":"c81671be-a12b-4d46-bff8-c8945d722a29","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a9a2405","slug":"virtual-meandering-taco","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Set up a Python virtual environment for the minisgl library at /app/minisgl/.venv and install all dependencies. Steps:\n1. Create the venv: python3 -m venv /app/minisgl/.venv\n2. First check if there's a setup.py or pyproject.toml: ls /app/minisgl/setup.py /app/minisgl/pyproject.toml /app/minisgl/requirements.txt 2>&1\n3. Check the structure: ls /app/minisgl/python/ 2>&1\n4. Install dependencies that minisgl needs (based on prior analysis): /app/minisgl/.venv/bin/pip install msgpack numpy torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu pyzmq transformers\n   NOTE: If torch CPU install fails with that index URL, try: /app/minisgl/.venv/bin/pip install msgpack numpy pyzmq transformers && /app/minisgl/.venv/bin/pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu\n   If that also fails, try: /app/minisgl/.venv/bin/pip install msgpack numpy pyzmq transformers torch\n5. If there's a setup.py or pyproject.toml, install minisgl: /app/minisgl/.venv/bin/pip install -e /app/minisgl\n   If not, the fuzz.py uses sys.path.insert so it should work without installation.\n6. Install atheris: /app/minisgl/.venv/bin/pip install atheris\n7. Verify: /app/minisgl/.venv/bin/python -c \"import msgpack; import numpy; import atheris; print('minisgl venv OK')\"\n\nIMPORTANT: This may take a while due to torch. Use timeouts of 600 seconds for pip commands.\n"},"uuid":"6a61ffcd-bedc-4113-88ba-f1e1396d588f","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:27:20.352Z"}
